  {
    "sha": "b5ba8ac00d64d38fd5b69714fe398b61c56d8160",
    "node_id": "C_kwDORgZXs9oAKGI1YmE4YWMwMGQ2NGQzOGZkNWI2OTcxNGZlMzk4YjYxYzU2ZDgxNjA",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "haosenwang1018",
        "email": "1293965075@qq.com",
        "date": "2026-03-09T15:51:02Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "haosenwang1018",
        "email": "1293965075@qq.com",
        "date": "2026-03-09T15:51:02Z"
      },
      "message": "fix NaN loss not caught by fast-fail check\n\n`train_loss_f > 100` silently passes on NaN because IEEE 754 NaN\ncomparisons always return False. When an agent experiment produces\nNaN (e.g. from an aggressive LR change), the run wastes the full\n5-minute budget instead of failing fast.\n\n`not (x <= 100)` catches both >100 and NaN with no added complexity.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "7a80512cac1e9abdff56ebc69b1a0df76318d7ba",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/karpathy/autoresearch/git/trees/7a80512cac1e9abdff56ebc69b1a0df76318d7ba"
      },
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/karpathy/autoresearch/git/commits/b5ba8ac00d64d38fd5b69714fe398b61c56d8160",
      "comment_count": 0,
      "verification": {
        "verified": false,
        "reason": "unsigned",
        "signature": null,
        "payload": null,
        "verified_at": null
      }
    },
